.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn EVP_PKEY_new
and
.Fn EVP_PKEY_free
functions exist in all versions of OpenSSL.
.Pp
The
.Fn EVP_PKEY_up_ref
function was added in OpenSSL 1.1.0.
.Pp
The
.Fn EVP_PKEY_new_raw_private_key ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_new_raw_public_key ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_new_CMAC_key ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_new_raw_private_key
and
.Fn EVP_PKEY_get_raw_public_key
functions were added in OpenSSL 1.1.1.
.Pp
The
.Fn EVP_PKEY_dup ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_new_raw_private_key_ex ,
and
.Fn EVP_PKEY_new_raw_public_key_ex
functions were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
.Pp
The
.Fn EVP_PKEY_new_CMAC_key
was deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0.
.Pp
The documentation of
.Vt EVP_PKEY
was amended in OpenSSL 3.0 to allow there to be the private part of the
keypair without the public part, where this was previously implied to be
disallowed.
.Pp
Support for
.Sy ML-DSA
and
.Sy ML-KEM
was added in OpenSSL 3.5.
